  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation EU-Caribbean Cooperation Facility+</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The action intents to establish a flexible, demand-driven, and rapid-response mechanism to support the implementation of the Global Gateway in the Caribbean. The Facility will strengthen policy dialogue with partner countries, foster engagement with the private sector, promote the dissemination of EU standards and expertise, and enhance the capacities of Caribbean stakeholders. It will also enable support for concrete preliminary actions that can be scaled up and can generate investment opportunities in priority areas of the Global Gateway. This will be achieved through targeted modalities such as technical assistance, regional seminars, studies, capacity building, sponsorship of regional events, and study visits both within the Caribbean and to Europe.The Facility will enable support for a broader range of actions, allowing for greater sectoral and geographic coverage. In this context, coordinated actions with the Overseas Countries and Territories (OCTs) will also be promoted, as they are key partners for Europe, reinforce the EU&#xbf;s regional presence and cooperation in a strategically area of Global Gateway.</narrative>
  </description>
